---
import CountryLayout from "../../layouts/CountryLayout.astro";
import CountryCard from "../../components/CountryCard.astro";
import { countries } from "../../data/countries";
import { getBaseUrl } from "../../utils/routing";

const baseUrl = getBaseUrl();
---

<CountryLayout
  title="Countries"
  description="Explore tax information for countries worldwide. Find income tax, VAT, corporate tax, and more."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Countries" }]}
>

   <section class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-hairline dark:border-overlay-lighter bg-surface dark:bg-surface/30 px-6 py-12 sm:px-10 sm:py-16 mb-8" aria-labelledby="countries-heading">
  <!-- Subtle Grid Pattern -->
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[linear-gradient(to_right,#8080801a_1px,transparent_1px),linear-gradient(to_bottom,#8080801a_1px,transparent_1px)] bg-[size:32px_32px] [mask-image:radial-gradient(ellipse_80%_80%_at_50%_0%,#000_70%,transparent_100%)]"></div>
  
  <!-- Ambient Glowing Orbs -->
  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 flex justify-center" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="absolute top-[-20%] left-[15%] h-[300px] w-[300px] rounded-full bg-primary/20 blur-[100px]"></div>
    <div class="absolute top-[10%] right-[15%] h-[250px] w-[250px] rounded-full bg-indigo-500/20 blur-[100px]"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
    <span class="inline-block rounded-full border border-primary/30 bg-primary/10 px-4 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary dark:text-primary-light mb-6 shadow-sm backdrop-blur-md">Global Tax Coverage</span>
    <h1 id="countries-heading" class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-on-primary sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl mb-6">
      <span data-i18n="countries.heading">Countries</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto" data-i18n="countries.comprehensive_tax_info" data-i18n-vars={JSON.stringify({ count: countries.length })}>
      Explore comprehensive tax information for {countries.length} countries.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Search and Grid moved to the top -->
<div class="mb-8">
     <div class="relative">
         <input
           type="text"
           id="country-search"
           placeholder="Search countries..."
           aria-label="Search countries"
           data-i18n-placeholder="countries.search_countries"
           class="form-input !pl-10"
         />
         <svg class="absolute left-3 top-1/2 h-5 w-5 text-muted -translate-y-1/2 dark:text-muted" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
           <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M21 21l-6-6m2-5a7 7 0 11-14 0 7 7 0 0114 0z" />
         </svg>
       </div>
       <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">Search by country name or continent to quickly find the tax calculators and guides you need. Results update instantly as you type.</p>
   </div>

   <div class="mb-8">
       <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary"><span data-i18n="countries.all_countries">All Countries</span></h2>
     <CountryCard
       countries={countries.map(c => ({
         slug: c.slug,
         name: c.name,
         flag: c.flag,
         continent: c.continent,
         overview: c.overview
       }))}
       searchQuery=""
       selectedContinent=""
     />
   </div>

   <div class="mb-12">
     <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">How to Use This Site</h2>
     <p class="text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">
       Finsiva is designed to make international tax research fast and intuitive. Start by selecting a country from the list above or using the search bar. Each country page provides an overview of the tax system, links to specialized calculators, and articles explaining local rules.
     </p>
     <p class="mt-4 text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">
       To calculate tax, enter your income, deductions, and other relevant figures into the calculator. Results update instantly as you type, and you can adjust inputs to see how different scenarios affect your liability. All calculations happen in your browser, so your data never leaves your device.
     </p>
     <p class="mt-4 text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">
       For deeper understanding, explore the <a href="/knowledge/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Knowledge Center</a> for definitions and explanations, or read the <a href="/blogs/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Tax Blog</a> for practical strategies. If you have questions, visit the <a href="/contact/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Contact</a> page.
     </p>
   </div>

   <div class="mb-12">
     <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Popular Destinations</h2>
     <p class="text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted mb-4">
       Our most visited country pages cover major economies with complex tax systems. Whether you are planning a move, managing remote income, or comparing regimes, these guides are a great place to start.
     </p>
     <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
       <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
         <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">United States</h3>
         <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">Federal and state income tax, capital gains, payroll taxes, and self-employment estimates for one of the world's most complex tax systems.</p>
         <a href="/countries/united-states/" class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Explore US Tax Guides</a>
       </div>
       <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
         <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">India</h3>
         <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">GST, TDS, income tax slabs, and deductions under both the old and new tax regimes for individuals and businesses.</p>
         <a href="/countries/india/" class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Explore India Tax Guides</a>
       </div>
       <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
         <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">United Kingdom</h3>
         <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">Income tax bands, National Insurance, capital gains tax, and dividend taxation for UK residents and non-residents.</p>
         <a href="/countries/united-kingdom/" class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Explore UK Tax Guides</a>
       </div>
       <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
         <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Singapore</h3>
         <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">Resident and non-resident income tax, tax reliefs, and corporate tax basics for one of Asia's leading financial hubs.</p>
         <a href="/countries/singapore/" class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Explore Singapore Tax Guides</a>
       </div>
       <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
         <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Hong Kong</h3>
         <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">Salaries tax, property tax, profits tax, and standard-rate calculations for Hong Kong's territorial tax system.</p>
         <a href="/countries/hong-kong/" class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Explore Hong Kong Tax Guides</a>
       </div>
       <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
         <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Malaysia</h3>
         <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">Income tax, RPGT, and sales tax calculators for residents and non-residents navigating Malaysia's progressive tax structure.</p>
         <a href="/countries/malaysia/" class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Explore Malaysia Tax Guides</a>
       </div>
     </div>
   </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (function() {
      var searchInput = document.getElementById('country-search');
      var countryData = [];
      
      document.querySelectorAll('.group').forEach(function(el) {
        var name = el.querySelector('h3')?.textContent || '';
        var continent = el.querySelector('.text-muted')?.textContent || '';
        var slugEl = el.getAttribute('href');
        countryData.push({
          name: name,
          continent: continent,
          element: el
        });
      });

      function filterCountries(query) {
        var q = query.toLowerCase().trim();
        countryData.forEach(function(data) {
          var match = !q || 
            data.name.toLowerCase().includes(q) || 
            data.continent.toLowerCase().includes(q);
          data.element.style.display = match ? '' : 'none';
        });
      }

      if (searchInput) {
        searchInput.addEventListener('input', function(e) {
          filterCountries(e.target.value);
        });
      }
    })();
  </script>

<div class="mt-12 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">The Psychology Behind Navigating your tax obligations</h2>
  <p>
    Let's be incredibly honest for a moment. When you're trying to understand <strong>your tax obligations</strong>, the sheer volume of bureaucratic jargon can feel entirely overwhelming. It’s not just about the numbers or the compliance—it's about the psychological weight of getting it right. Fear of penalties, the stress of audits, and the anxiety of misinterpreting complex regulations are universal pain points.
  </p>
  <p>
    Many taxpayers and business owners experience what financial psychologists call "compliance fatigue." You are expected to be an expert in everything from withholding rules to obscure deduction clauses. The truth is, mastering your tax obligations requires a shift in mindset: from reactive compliance to proactive wealth preservation.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-6">Advanced Strategies for Minimizing Risk</h3>
  <p>
    Beyond the basic rules, the most successful individuals and corporations employ advanced, legally sound strategies. Here is how you can move from surviving to thriving:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
    <li><strong>Documentation is Your Shield:</strong> Never rely on memory. Maintain granular, digitized records of all expenses, receipts, and correspondence. A well-organized ledger is your best defense against arbitrary assessments.</li>
    <li><strong>Strategic Timing:</strong> The timing of income recognition and expense realization can drastically alter your tax footprint. Accelerating deductions or deferring income into the next fiscal period is a cornerstone of intelligent planning.</li>
    <li><strong>Professional Consultation over DIY:</strong> The cost of an expert is almost always lower than the cost of a compliance error. Navigating your tax obligations without professional counsel is an unnecessary risk.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-6">Troubleshooting Common Edge-Case Scenarios</h3>
  <p>
    What happens when things don't go according to plan? Let's address some edge cases that frequently trip up even seasoned professionals when dealing with your tax obligations:
  </p>
  <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
    <li><strong>Discrepancies in Source Documents:</strong> If a withholding certificate or an income statement contains errors, do not adjust your return to match the error. Request a formal correction from the issuer immediately.</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-Jurisdictional Conflicts:</strong> If your income crosses borders, you may face double taxation. Always invoke the relevant Double Taxation Avoidance Agreements (DTAA) and ensure you have the necessary tax residency certificates on hand.</li>
    <li><strong>Late Filing Repercussions:</strong> If you miss a deadline, the worst action is inaction. File as soon as possible and proactively request a waiver of penalties citing reasonable cause, if applicable.</li>
  </ol>

  <p class="mt-6 font-medium">
    Ultimately, navigating these regulations is a marathon, not a sprint. By prioritizing structured planning and mental clarity, you can turn a compliance burden into a strategic advantage.
  </p>
</div>

<!-- SEO Content moved to the bottom -->
<div class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-hairline dark:border-overlay-lighter">
  <div class="mb-12">
     <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Why Tax Information Matters</h2>
     <p class="text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">
       Understanding tax obligations is one of the most important aspects of personal and business finance. Whether you are a local resident, an expatriate, a freelancer, or a business owner, knowing how much you owe, when payments are due, and what deductions you can claim helps you avoid penalties, maximize refunds, and plan for the future.
     </p>
     <p class="mt-4 text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">
       Tax systems vary significantly from country to country. Progressive income tax in one nation may contrast sharply with a flat-rate regime in another. Value-added tax thresholds, property tax assessments, and capital gains treatment all differ based on local laws. Our goal is to present these differences clearly so you can make informed decisions wherever you live or work.
     </p>
     <p class="mt-4 text-body leading-relaxed dark:text-muted">
       Accurate tax information also supports compliance. Missing a filing deadline or misunderstanding residency rules can lead to avoidable interest charges or audits. By providing up-to-date calculators and guides, we help you stay on top of obligations without needing expensive software or professional consultations for basic scenarios.
     </p>
   </div>
</div>


</CountryLayout>
